 "title": "SIRT1 and Metabolic Regulation in Pancreatic β-cells",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around the gene or protein SIRT1 and its role in regulating metabolism, particularly in pancreatic β-cells. SIRT1 is activated by AMPK and regulates various genes and processes, including energy metabolism, PGC-1α, and FOXO3a. It also downregulates UCP2 and regulates GLUT4 and Glut2. SIRT1's activation is mediated by resveratrol and SRT2104, and it is involved in the regulation of pancreatic β-cells. Additionally, SIRT1 is linked to the process of metabolism and is affected by calorie restriction. The cluster also includes other genes and processes related to metabolism and pancreatic β-cell regulation, such as AMPK, PGC-1α, and NGN3.",
